// Single source of truth for the platform's India state → city taxonomy.
// Replaces the old flat ~7-city "metro only" lists that used to be hardcoded
// separately (and inconsistently) in three different frontend pages. See
// frontend/lib/locations.ts for the mirror.
//
// Selection is two-step: pick a state/UT, then pick one or more cities within
// it.
//
// As of 2026-09-17: 3,845 unique towns/cities across all 36 states and UTs
// (up from 1,801), sourced from each state's official urban local body
// roster (Municipal Corporations, Councils, Nagar Panchayats — Wikipedia's
// per-state "List of urban local bodies in X" / tehsil-list articles mirror
// state government gazette data) rather than hand-picked district
// headquarters, per client feedback that the list should go as deep as a
// telecom coverage checker's — every town someone might actually live in,
// not just the well-known ones. It is still not literally every census
// town or village in India (that's tens of thousands more, mostly places
// too small to have their own urban body); if a specific town is still
// missing, add it here and mirror the same addition in
// frontend/lib/locations.ts.
// City values already stored on old records (all metro names) are preserved
// verbatim inside their correct state so legacy data keeps matching.

